ng  this i didn't tell anyone i kept it a  secret  yep and you only could tell them after  they started to wonder like what the  hell is tj doing  i'm fairly certain my family assumed i  was leading a double life  which i guess i was but just you know  not in the way that they necessarily  expected look i had come off of several  years in new york pursuing a career in  theater  and it was nothing but failure  i mean just failure after failure after  failure and so when i  left new york i kind of turned a little  bit more  introverted in that way of of risks that  i put out there and that's why i didn't  tell anybody i was writing this book  i wanted to do it for me falling joins a  list of airplane-based thrillers that  first took off  with arthur haley's best-selling 1968  novel  airport you'll kill yourself for nothing  if you explode that bomb  stay where you're from when it was made  into a hit movie in 1970  it spawned a whole new genre of disaster  films  and spoofs passengers certain to die  airline negligence there's a sail at  pennies  none more famous than 1980s airplane can  you fly this plane and land it  surely you can't be serious i am serious  and don't call me shirley  ever since hollywood and the publishing  world have had a long track record of  cashing in on the high anxiety world of  air travel  i have had it with these snakes on this  plane i remember reading a michael  crichton book that was scary incidents  regarding planes and you'd think it  would make people more scared to fly  it actually made me more comfortable  airframe is the book and i love that  book and  that's a response that i've gotten from  from falling as well which  surprised me but i love people have said  you know  i've typically been terrified to fly i'm  a horrible flyer but reading this book i  feel reassured because i didn't know  there were so many options falling will  likely change the way you think next  time you do step on a plane  as newman hammers home hint making sure  your drink is topped off  is not what a flight attendant is there  for it's so nice to have the job viewed  from a more  respectful position now that said the  food and drinks and all that is  is part of it but it's not mainly what  you're there for no  we i mean service is just something we  gladly provide  but you'll almost never see flight  attendants doing their job i hope you  never see us doing our job because our  job is to make sure  if there's a medical emergency we're  handling it  if you're having a heart attack i'm not  going to bring you a diet coke i'm going  to go get the defibrillator  and make sure that you survive flight  attendants are on board for safety and  security  period last year newman took a voluntary  furlough from her flight attendant  duties  recently she quit outright her job  flying is done but it sounds like  writing about planes  is not i flew for 10 years so i don't  think i exhausted all of my  stories and experience in one book so i  might have a  at least a couple more you know surreal  is a word that gets overused and  you know there's there's so many cliches  associated with sort of finding  sudden success in publishing but have  you  have you gotten more comfortable with it  surreal is overused and overused by me i  say it probably multiple times a day but  i don't know  a better word to describe what i'm  feeling this doesn't feel real  i got so used to hearing and accepting  no that it's hard for me to accept that  the yeses are actually happening that  i'm here that this is actually  coming to pass it is surreal  i'm happy for you thank you  we're happy too jeff it's so good it  moves  it it just moves at a great pace it's  it's it's a great b treat it's a great  thriller  i can't wait to see the movie i love her  story because  clearly she saw failure as a path  to success i mean it's just so great  that she  kept moving forward yep after 41  rejections can you imagine her sketching  out the ideas in the cockpit  no it's awesome it's awesome and  thanks for the airplane clip too yes and  snakes on a plane  and air force one and airport  how about that

